WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:01.117
All you can eat.

00:00:01.127 --> 00:00:02.258
For a dollar.

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.714
Las Vegas, 1946:

00:00:03.724 --> 00:00:07.272
a midnight buffet, one fixed price.

00:00:07.372 --> 00:00:10.196
El Rancho Vegas, the first casino on

00:00:10.206 --> 00:00:11.674
what became the Strip.

00:00:11.684 --> 00:00:14.199
First the Chuck Wagon, later the Buckaroo

00:00:14.209 --> 00:00:15.067
Buffet.

00:00:15.077 --> 00:00:17.600
The casino almost certainly lost money on

00:00:17.610 --> 00:00:17.984
it.

00:00:17.994 --> 00:00:20.427
Yet casinos all over town copied it.

00:00:20.437 --> 00:00:21.131
Why?

00:00:21.141 --> 00:00:23.266
So nobody had to leave.

00:00:23.291 --> 00:00:26.056
Fed gamblers went straight
back to gambling,

00:00:26.066 --> 00:00:28.316
and the house won while they played.
